---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — HighJack"
  description="Why HighJack exists: a configurable, deterministic, multiplayer board/economy game built in the open."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="m-0 font-display text-3xl font-extrabold sm:text-4xl">About HighJack</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 mb-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      HighJack started with a simple frustration: classic property-board games are brilliant social
      machines locked inside one fixed rulebook. We want the table — and the option to rig it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl" aria-label="Project story">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-md leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      <p>
        The name is the thesis. <strong class="text-gold-400">HIGH</strong> — the rush of a stack
        growing, a card lifting off the table, the jackpot direction.
        <strong class="text-gold-400">JACK</strong> — the pot, the prize, and the polite little
        crime of taking both from someone else. One word, two directions of greed.
      </p>
      <p>
        So the design goal became a game where the group decides what kind of evening it's having:
        pure economic siege, or property empire laced with poker nights, carnival side-bets, and
        global events that rain chaos on everyone equally. Every system is a switch. The engine
        doesn't care which ones you flip — it just runs your table fairly.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-0">
        Fairly is the operative word. HighJack is built around an authoritative deterministic
        simulation: outcomes are computed once, server-side, from seeds and actions anyone can
        re-verify. Play-money only, forever — this is a game about risking fake fortunes with real
        friends, not a casino.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
    <h2 id="stack-title" class="m-0 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold">
      Built with
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display font-bold text-cream-100">Astro + SolidJS</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-1 text-sm text-muted-400">
          Static-first website; islands only where interaction earns it.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display font-bold text-cream-100">PixiJS</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-1 text-sm text-muted-400">
          GPU-rendered boards and pieces behind the application UI.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display font-bold text-cream-100">Go 1.26</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-1 text-sm text-muted-400">
          Authoritative engine and realtime server as a modular monolith.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-surface-raised p-5 shadow-card">
        <h3 class="m-0 font-display font-bold text-cream-100">Bun</h3>
        <p class="mb-0 mt-1 text-sm text-muted-400">
          One toolchain for workspaces, tests, and builds.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="mt-12 max-w-3xl rounded-lg border border-line-subtle bg-felt-900/60 p-6"
    aria-label="Open source"
  >
    <h2 class="m-0 font-display text-lg font-bold text-cream-100">Open by default</h2>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-400">
      The whole project — engine, protocol, tooling, and this site — is MIT-licensed and developed
      in the open at
      <a
        href="https://github.com/analeis/highjack"
        class="font-bold text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-500"
      >
        github.com/analeis/highjack
      </a>
      . Architecture decisions live in the repository's docs, so every choice is inspectable.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
